3) KEY FEATURES (PRODUCT/DOMAIN)
From Project Brief, Architecture, Domain Model, and API Spec:
- Tour operations are destination-first with nights and computed arrival/departure flow.
- Each destination supports 5 service groups:
  1. Accommodation
  2. Meals
  3. Guide
  4. Local Transport
  5. Intercity Transport
- Per-item communication threads support outbound/inbound message logging.
- Booking-to-task automation is planned (booked state triggers task generation/reminders).
- Itinerary composer aggregates destination text + service blocks + media into output.
- MVP UX direction: 3 tabs (Tour Config, Pricing Config, Visual).

4) CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION STATUS (CODE)
- src/index.js currently exposes demo endpoints:
  - /message -> Hello, World!
  - /random -> UUID
  - default -> 404 Not Found
- test/index.spec.js validates /message and /random in unit + integration style tests.
- Existing tests are aligned with current demo worker behavior.

5) DATA MODEL CONTEXT
D1 schema exists in db/seeds.sql with tables covering:
- tenancy and user management: tenants, users, memberships
- tours and route points: tours, destinations, destination_texts
- 5 service item groups:
  - dest_accommodations
  - dest_meals
  - dest_guides
  - dest_local_transports
  - dest_intercity_legs
- commercial and presentation:
  - tour_prices
  - tour_policies
  - tour_visuals
  - tour_media
- communications and operations:
  - comm_threads
  - comm_messages
  - tasks

Seed dataset includes Vietnam demo content:
- tenant demo-agency
- owner user
- one sample tour: Vietnam Essentials (HCMC-HN-SP) 6N5D
- three destinations: Sai Gon, Ha Noi, Sa Pa
- sample records for all major service types
- sample pricing/policy/visual/media/task and comm message

